# Graphify — derived output, ~7 MB across ~1200 generated JSON/HTML files that
# git compresses poorly and nobody reviews. `graphify update .` rebuilds all of
# it from the source tree in seconds, AST-only, with no API key involved.
#
# Nothing here is kept, the community labels included. They were tracked for a
# while on the theory that `graphify label` spends an LLM call and a fresh clone
# would have to pay for it again. Reading the file settles it: the labels are
# file and symbol names lifted from the AST — "anime.controller.ts",
# "compilerOptions" — and every run reports that no Gemini key is configured, so
# no model has ever named anything. What they did cost was churn: the file
# changed in 7 of this branch's 20 commits, adding a diff nobody reads to a
# third of its pull request.
graphify-out/
